Similarly, the most significant factor in evaluating the situation is how private dehumanization can become normalized, making it easier for others to repeat such behavior and weakening group solidarity (Option A). Intent and context are relevant but secondary; the potential for broader harm outweighs the nuance of private intent (Option C). Excluding private speech from the moral domain (Option B) contradicts the collective view that all actions reflecting on the community matter.

